ifest_entry_rejected"},{"id":"spn-49741","text":", "},{"id":"spn-49742","marks":["code"],"text":"test_extra_verifier_evidence_rejected"},{"id":"spn-49743","text":"."}]},{"id":"blk-33883","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-49744","text":"Step 5 — exact contract "},{"id":"spn-49745","marks":["bold"],"text":"and"},{"id":"spn-49746","text":" implementation version match → "},{"id":"spn-49747","marks":["code"],"text":"unavailable"}]},{"id":"blk-33884","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-49748","marks":["code"],"text":"fresh_versions"},{"id":"spn-49749","text":" is built from the reward's contracts + the wired verifiers' implementations, driven by what the receipt sealed: a scored signal whose sealed implementation is "},{"id":"spn-49750","marks":["code"],"text":"null"},{"id":"spn-49751","text":" was UNWIRED at eval time and stays unwired (→ "},{"id":"spn-49752","marks":["code"],"text":"not_applicable"},{"id":"spn-49753","text":", no spurious mismatch); a non-null sealed implementation must be reproduced by an available verifier "},{"id":"spn-49754","marks":["bold"],"text":"of the same version"},{"id":"spn-49755","text":", else "},{"id":"spn-49756","marks":["code"],"text":"checks[\"verifier_versions\"].ok = False"},{"id":"spn-49757","text":" → "},{"id":"spn-49758","marks":["bold"],"text":"outcome `unavailable` (exit 2)"},{"id":"spn-49759","text":", never an evidence failure."}]},{"id":"blk-33885","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-49760","text":"Battery: "},{"id":"spn-49761","marks":["code"],"text":"test_verifier_implementation_drift_is_unavailable"},{"id":"spn-49762","text":"."}]},{"id":"blk-33886","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-49763","text":"Step 6 — persist + replay policy-violation evidence (REVERSES the prior ruling)"}]},{"id":"blk-33887","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-49764","marks":["code"],"text":"_populate"},{"id":"spn-49765","text":" writes "},{"id":"spn-49766","marks":["code"],"text":"evidence/process/policy-violations.json"},{"id":"spn-49767","text":". Replay loads it, re-attests it against the trace's "},{"id":"spn-49768","marks":["code"],"text":"policy_violations_digest"},{"id":"spn-49769","text":", and sets "},{"id":"spn-49770","marks":["code"],"text":"tampered = bool(violations)"},{"id":"spn-49771","text":" — feeding "},{"id":"spn-49772","marks":["code"],"text":"build_receipt_v1"},{"id":"spn-49773","text":" so the derived receipt reproduces the tamper verdict. (This reverses the prior \"score the un-tampered path\" decision you rejected.)"}]},{"id":"blk-33888","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-49774","text":"Battery: "},{"id":"spn-49775","marks":["code"],"text":"test_authentic_tampered_episode_reverifies_invalid"},{"id":"spn-49776","text":" (a real policy violation → the bundle CLOSES, sealed + derived receipts both read "},{"id":"spn-49777","marks":["code"],"text":"invalid"},{"id":"spn-49778","text":"), "},{"id":"spn-49779","marks":["code"],"text":"test_policy_violation_bytes_match_trace_digest"},{"id":"spn-49780","text":"."}]},{"id":"blk-33889","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-49781","text":"Step 7 — preserve snapshot file modes on materialization"}]},{"id":"blk-33890","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-49782","text":"New "},{"id":"spn-49783","marks":["code"],"text":"admission.materialize_subject(snapshot, content, root)"},{"id":"spn-49784","text":" restores each path's sealed "},{"id":"spn-49785","marks":["code"],"text":"file_modes"},{"id":"spn-49786","text":" (default "},{"id":"spn-49787","marks":["code"],"text":"0644"},{"id":"spn-49788","text":"), so a "},{"id":"spn-49789","marks":["code"],"text":"0755"},{"id":"spn-49790","text":" executable survives persistence and re-admits. "},{"id":"spn-49791","marks":["code"],"text":"_populate"},{"id":"spn-49792","text":" uses it instead of the runner's umask-dropping writer."}]},{"id":"blk-33891","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-49793","text":"Battery: "},{"id":"spn-49794","marks":["code"],"text":"tes